The PowerGlove Serial Interface (PGSI) Project Archive

This file is archived on ftp.acm.uiuc.edu in  /pub/pgsi/README

A project of the Special Interest Group for Computer Architecture
(SIGARCH), Student Chapter of the Association for Computing Machinery
at the University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign (ACM at UIUC).

The documentation is currently version 0.3

Note: This version of the user's manual is somewhat out of date.  We will be
updating it soon for the second run.

File  	      	      	Description
----  	      	      	-----------

---Documentation
README	      	      	This file
README.sgi-samples      Info file on basic source for Personal Iris

pgsi-faq      	      	The Frequently Asked Questions file for the PGSI
pgsi-history  	      	A short history of the PGSI
pgsi-order-form	      	Information on how to order your very own PGSI

pgsi-doc-wfw2 	      	PGSI documentation in Microsoft Word for Windows format
pgsi-doc-ascii 	      	PGSI documentation in ASCII format
pgsi-doc-ps 	      	PGSI documentation in postscript format
pgsi-doc-rtf 	      	PGSI documentation in Rich Text Format format
pgsi-doc-mw4 	      	PGSI documentation in Microsoft Word for Mac format
pg-faq	      	      	The Frequently Asked Questions file for the PowerGlove
pg-timing.gif 	      	PowerGlove Timing diagram in gif format

---Applications


DIRECTORY /mac

This directory contains sample programs and code that run on the Macintosh
and support the PGSI.

README.PGtheMouse	Info file on Mac mouse Driver for the PGSI
PGtheMouse.sea.hqx	PG the Mouse application

DIRECTORY /pc

README.maestro2      	Info file on Maestro II virtual keyboard instrument
README.develop5		Info file on REND386 hacked to work with the PGSI
README.maestro2		Info file on virtual keyboard instrument for windows
README.gerlt-sample	Info file on sample source for PGSI on PCs in C++
maestro2.zip		Zipped Maestro II application
devel5.zip		REND386 hack for the PGSI
pgsisega.zip            This .ZIP file contains mods to sgsppt.c to support
      	      	      	the PGSI sega glasses output within REND386. 
gerlt-sample		Sample code for getting data from the PGSI on the PC

DIRECTORY /sgi

sgi-samples.tar.Z     	Basic Personal Iris code for PGSA (PGSI)


DIRECTORY /pictures

---Artwork
"PGSI_logo is the gloved had reaching into a moniter screen, and PGSI_logo_anti
is the same picture with some of the lines "smeared" (not true antialiasing,
but same effect).

The tiffs are in full 24 bit color, and the gifs are what XV decided was a good
dither of them.  I would disagree, but that was the software at hand...

The gifs aren't compressed because that makes them bigger."
 -Jay Kreibich

PGSI_logo.xxx           PGSI logo in xxx format
PGSI_logo_anti.xxx    	PGSI logo in xxx format, antialiased

Please mail any questions, problems, or suggestions to pgsi@uiuc.edu
